==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[Hallowe'en]]

===Etymology===
A shortening of ''[[All Hallows'|All-Hallow]]-[[even#Etymology 3|even]]'', ''All Hallows’ Eve'' (the name of the evening before [[All Saints Day]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌhæləˈwiːn/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌhæləˈwin/|/ˌhɑləˈwin/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[eve]] of [[All Hallows' Day]]; 31st [[October]]; celebrated (mostly in the [[United Kingdom]], [[Canada]], [[United States]] and [[Ireland]]) by [[children]] going [[door-to-door]] in [[costume]] and demanding [[candy]] with [[menace]]s.

